mod:pointer_targets_deep;
// A POINTER'S TARGETS PAST THE WALKS' REACH ARE REFUSED (DEF-430's own walks, landing 177d2b4). `pointer_targets_of` resolves a pointer through
// the pointers below it, one fuel each (8), and `targets_held` reads what a holder holds, holder by holder (its own 16, counting the pointer
// locals below a pointer level and then the holders). Each answered "nothing more" at its end, so a write through the pointer freed a string
// under a by-value copy that read it after: `pt_chain_9` (9 pointers), `th_nest_17` (17 holders), `th_mix_10_8` (10 holders of 2 fields under
// 8 pointers: 7 pointer locals and 10 holders), `wn_9` (a view of `s` taken through 9 pointers, `s` written by its own name), each 83 and 97
// under the freed-heap detector on 000c645; `ln_9` (a spawn lent `s`'s arena through 9 pointers, `s` assigned over) was accepted there, where 8
// is BORROW-016. Each end refuses now, BORROW-007, at the place its caller is checking: the write through the pointer (`pt_chain_9`,
// `th_nest_17`), the write by name (`wn_9`), the spawn's pointer (`ln_9`). Where the caller refuses that place itself, its report is the one
// (`th_mix_10_8`: BORROW-015 at the write, D-240). `sl_9` has two mistakes on one line, and two reports: the end's, and BORROW-015 at the write
// of `t`, which doesn't hold it. The controls one under each end are `pointer_targets_deep_ok.npk`.
error:E5;
